## Flags

**`STAB_SATURATED` (bit 0)**  
Set when the pre‑saturation stability width exceeded 65535; not set if it is exactly 65535.  
**`FLAG_AVOID` (bit 1)**  
Detrimental resonance: the candidate failed a detrimental threshold (jitter or advance regularity).  
**`FLAG_SKIPPED` (bit 2)**  
The candidate was intentionally not evaluated because it lies in a `SKIP_ZONE` or an inter‑zone gap.  
**`FLAG_INVALID` (bit 3)**  
The candidate could not be evaluated (zero advance, N‑search failure, `N > MAX_N`, long‑term iteration exhaustion, or no valid jitter points). Always set together with `FLAG_AVOID`.  
**`FLAG_CENTRAL_ABOVE` (bit 4)**  
The central total time was strictly greater than `reference_block_time`.  
**`FLAG_CENTRAL_BELOW` (bit 5)**  
The central total time was strictly less than `reference_block_time`.  
Bits 6–7 are reserved and must be zero.

